Author: Nick Hung <nick@andestech.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 9 19:28:34 2026 +0800

    structural: simplify F7 run --model fast (no behavior change)

    /simplify cleanup of the F7 diff; all driver unit tests + f1-f7 acceptance
    (incl. real qemu+vsim) stay green.

    - run_fast resolves qemu via the now-exposed builtin_qemu() instead of
      discover_engines(), which scanned verilator/build and spawned a `--describe`
      subprocess per Verilator binary (5 here; up to N*5s on a hung one) only to
      discard them all -- wasted startup latency on every fast run, including
      interactive gdbstub launches. This also deletes cmd_run's copy of
      find_engine (duplicated run_plan.cpp's) and an unreachable `!qemu` guard.
    - check_eq, byte-identical in run_test.cpp and plan_test.cpp, moves to the
      shared test_check.hpp; both test files now `using andes_sim::test::check_eq`.
    - cmd_run returns run_passthrough's rc on an argv-build failure instead of
      discarding it and returning its own 2 -- one source of truth for that exit.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

